WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.751 --> 00:00:14.731
looked at me intently.

2
00:00:15.591 --> 00:00:17.852
I realized he was signaling me to keep quiet.

3
00:00:18.712 --> 00:00:21.733
Apparently the young woman was not yet ready to reveal her identity.

4
00:00:22.513 --> 00:00:25.734
The boys ran down to the sailboat for the things we needed to make camp.

5
00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:30.395
While my wife hurried to prepare supper, my sons entertained the stranger.

6
00:00:31.236 --> 00:00:35.189
By the time we sat down to supper, the young woman was laughing and chatting merrily.

7
00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:40.051
But she never mentioned her past life or why she was dressed as a naval officer.

8
00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.612
We made up a bed for her on the sailboat.

9
00:00:43.232 --> 00:00:46.774
When she retired for the night, Jack threw another log on our fire.

10
00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:49.235
"All right, Fritz," said Jack.

11
00:00:49.255 --> 00:00:51.876
"Tell us where you found this jolly fellow.

12
00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:53.657
Did you meet him by chance?

13
00:00:54.037 --> 00:00:56.718
Or did you go in search of him on your mysterious voyage?"

14
00:00:57.478 --> 00:01:01.900
Fritz hesitated a moment, and then told the story of the message tied to the albatross.

15
00:01:02.824 --> 00:01:05.086
"When I left you, I paddled for two days.

16
00:01:05.907 --> 00:01:08.549
I was beginning to lose hope that I would find the Englishwoman."

17
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.993
"That albatross could have flown hundreds of miles before it reached you," said Ernest.

18
00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:15.896
"That's why I was discouraged," said Fritz.

19
00:01:16.797 --> 00:01:19.339
"Finally a high section of land came into view.

20
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.642
When I rounded it, I found a calm and pleasant bay.

21
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.285
And I saw a column of smoke rising from the rocky shore!

22
00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:29.308
I realized it was the 'smoking rock' in the message."

23
00:01:30.396 --> 00:01:31.617
"What did you do next?"

24
00:01:31.977 --> 00:01:32.597
asked Franz.

25
00:01:33.398 --> 00:01:36.579
"As soon as I landed, I spotted Miss Montrose coming toward me."

26
00:01:36.599 --> 00:01:38.641
"What?" cried Jack.

27
00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:41.342
"Don't you mean Mister Montrose?"

28
00:01:41.682 --> 00:01:42.303
said Franz.

29
00:01:42.323 --> 00:01:44.664
"Oh, Fritz," said Ernest.

30
00:01:44.684 --> 00:01:47.285
"I guessed Edward Montrose was a young woman."

31
00:01:48.646 --> 00:01:52.428
"She's embarrassed that she doesn't have any proper clothing," Fritz explained.

32
00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:56.730
"I can take care of that as soon as we return to Rockburg," Mother said.

33
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.392
"Now please tell us her real name."

34
00:02:00.212 --> 00:02:02.393
"Her name is Jenny Montrose," said Fritz.

35
00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:06.576
"She's the daughter of a British army officer, and she was born in India."

36
00:02:07.336 --> 00:02:08.597
He continued with her story.

37
00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.338
Jenny's mother had died when she was three.

38
00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:16.001
After his wife's death, Colonel Montrose focused all his attention on Jenny.

39
00:02:16.861 --> 00:02:20.443
She became an accomplished rider and shared his interest in the outdoors.

40
00:02:21.324 --> 00:02:25.466
When Colonel Montrose received orders to return to England, he sent Jenny ahead.

41
00:02:26.327 --> 00:02:28.528
A storm hit her ship a week after it left India.

42
00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.382
Everyone was forced to abandon ship and board the lifeboats.

43
00:02:33.362 --> 00:02:36.924
All the lifeboats disappeared and finally Jenny's boat capsized.

44
00:02:37.685 --> 00:02:39.466
She was the only person to reach shore.

45
00:02:39.486 --> 00:02:46.469
"From that moment three years ago, until I found her, she never saw another human being," said Fritz.

46
00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:50.191
"She kept a fire burning, hoping to attract a passing ship.

47
00:02:50.932 --> 00:02:53.873
And she caught and tamed birds so that she could send messages with them."

48
00:02:54.554 --> 00:02:55.074
He went on.

49
00:02:55.094 --> 00:03:00.473
"She greeted me with tears in her eyes and said, 'Thank goodness you have come at last!

50
00:03:01.354 --> 00:03:04.216
I've waited impatiently since the bird returned with your message.'"

51
00:03:04.997 --> 00:03:08.759
"But how did she manage to live by herself for so many years?"

52
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.861
asked my wife, full of concern.

53
00:03:10.881 --> 00:03:13.443
"She is quite clever," said Fritz.

54
00:03:14.303 --> 00:03:17.706
"Some tools and a chest of navy uniforms washed ashore from the wreck.

55
00:03:18.446 --> 00:03:22.329
With these she managed to build a hut on the ground and a safe sleeping place in a

56
00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:25.952
tree. She had also made bows, arrows, and fish hooks.

57
00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.789
So she was able to provide food for herself."

58
00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:32.370
"She is a clever girl indeed," said my wife.

59
00:03:33.331 --> 00:03:35.271
We went to sleep on board the sailboat that night.

60
00:03:36.052 --> 00:03:38.053
The next morning we all assembled for breakfast.

61
00:03:38.853 --> 00:03:40.213
I addressed Miss Montrose.

62
00:03:40.233 --> 00:03:43.455
"There is no need to hide your identity," I said.

63
00:03:43.475 --> 00:03:45.836
"We welcome you just as you are."

64
00:03:46.616 --> 00:03:47.396
Jenny smiled.

65
00:03:47.416 --> 00:03:49.977
"The boys were treating me differently this morning.

66
00:03:49.997 --> 00:03:53.579
"So I thought you must have guessed my secret.

67
00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:55.980
I shouldn't be ashamed of these clothes.

68
00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.122
In women's clothes I wouldn't have been able to manage all the work I had to do."

69
00:04:00.943 --> 00:04:02.684
After breakfast we started for Rockburg.

70
00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:05.306
Fritz and Jack went ahead in the kayak.

71
00:04:06.086 --> 00:04:10.049
When we arrived, they led the way through the gardens, orchards, and shrubs.

72
00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.752
Jenny was amazed when we arrived at Rockburg itself.

73
00:04:13.772 --> 00:04:17.234
"I cannot believe that all this exists!"

74
00:04:17.714 --> 00:04:18.815
She looked around in wonder.

75
00:04:19.476 --> 00:04:23.078
Jack and Fritz had set the table outside and laid out a fine meal.

76
00:04:23.779 --> 00:04:25.660
There was even a vase of flowers on the table.

77
00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.302
"Come inside and change before we eat," said my wife.

78
00:04:30.023 --> 00:04:32.325
When Jenny returned, she looked prettier than ever.

79
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.588
I motioned her to sit between my wife and me.

80
00:04:36.388 --> 00:04:40.151
Ernest and Franz also sat, but Fritz and Jack wanted to wait on us all.

81
00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:42.533
"What a perfect feast!"

82
00:04:43.094 --> 00:04:45.315
said Jenny with tears of joy in her eyes.
